# Copy to $CONTROLLER_HOME/remote-gate-weights.tsv (or point CONTROLLER_REMOTE_WEIGHTS_FILE at it).
# <project-dir>:<lane><TAB><measured peak MiB of the lane container (or slice) on the gate worker>
# remote-gate.sh weighs a lane as min(declared resources.memory, measured peak * 1.15); the weight, rounded up to
# whole slots (budget / slots MiB each), is how many of the worker's flock slots the lane takes.
# R2-class lanes (r2, mutation, self-qualification*, campaign) are deliberately NOT listed: their weight is the declared
# cap (workers grow over a long run). An unlisted, undeclared lane takes one slot (two for an R2-class name).
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. The numbers below are examples, not measurements to rely on.
project-a:r1	997
project-b:selftest	1073
project-c:tooling-tests	567
